# Try the API from Visual Studio, Rider or VS Code (REST Client). Start the stack first:
#   docker compose up --build
@baseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### Place an order. Send it twice: the second response is 200 with the same order, not a duplicate.
# @name placeOrder
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-order-001

{
  "customerId": "0193a5b2-7c41-7d2e-9f10-3c5e8a1b2d4f",
  "currency": "NZD",
  "lines": [
    { "sku": "KEYBOARD", "quantity": 2, "unitPrice": 89.50 },
    { "sku": "MOUSE", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 25.00 }
  ]
}

###
@orderId = {{placeOrder.response.body.$.id}}

### Read it back
GET {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}

### Act as the payments service: publish PaymentCapturedV1 to RabbitMQ (Development only).
# The order becomes Paid asynchronously, through the consumer and the idempotent inbox.
POST {{baseUrl}}/dev/payments
Content-Type: application/json

{ "orderId": "{{orderId}}", "amount": 204.00, "currency": "NZD", "paymentId": "pay_demo_001" }

### Ship it (only valid once paid)
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders/{{orderId}}/ship
Content-Type: application/json

{ "trackingNumber": "NZ000123456" }

### Validation failure: an RFC 9457 problem with a machine-readable "code"
POST {{baseUrl}}/orders
Content-Type: application/json
Idempotency-Key: demo-invalid-001

{ "customerId": "0193a5b2-7c41-7d2e-9f10-3c5e8a1b2d4f", "currency": "NZD", "lines": [ { "sku": "not a sku", "quantity": 1, "unitPrice": 1 } ] }

### Readiness: PostgreSQL, RabbitMQ and outbox lag
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
